w and the single startup-authority owner are unchanged. Proven by the consumer-parity witness extended with a non-hosting joiner whose getPublication yields no routable candidate while its system-table cache holds the authority-published row: red on HEAD (formationReleaseHandoff null, barrier waits on the raw spread predicate), green after (state active, releaseAuthorized true, barrier ledger_spread_satisfied within the retained generation). Root cause from the 9d5deb4f1 GCP streak: all seven contract consumptions since 9c4fd323c were by cpp-hosting joiners; non-hosting joiners polled an active, authorized contract for 3-35 s without consuming (07-06-30: n4 released raw at W+68.0; 07-13-07: n3/n4 never).","title":null,"class":"product","constraints":[{"id":"source-change-subagent-verification","statement":"If this Quest changes source code, spawn a subagent verifier before audit and git handoff, then record a Solver finding with evidence subagent:<id>."},{"id":"single-formation-release-owner","statement":"The seed-owned formation-release handoff closure owner remains the sole minting authority; the joiner projection reads and validates, never mints or re-derives release authority; the publication read exemption is scoped to this consumer read of the authority publication."},{"id":"validation-before-release","statement":"A row obtained through the exempt durable read or the cached fallback is consumed only after validateFormationReleaseHandoffConsumerContract in the CONSUMER role; no path lets an unvalidated or stale row reach releaseAuthorized. Fail-closed cases (different authority incarnation, regressed epoch, revoked generation, cohort outside the canonical set, restarted joiner) stay null."},{"id":"unchanged-budgets-and-owner-rules","statement":"Seed capture/retention/revocation, the consumer validation predicates, the 60-second GCP certification window and the 120-second internal barrier, readiness floors, polling cadences and the single startup-authority owner